+/*
+ * Apple SoCs have no PSCI firmware, and pdArmHaltRestart's PSCI probe walks
+ * the IORegistry, whose locks may not be taken from the panic path. No Apple
+ * reset driver exists here yet, so install no handler: PE_halt_restart stays
+ * NULL, IOPlatformExpert::haltRestart() returns -1, and halt_all_cpus() spins
+ * once pd_psci_halt() finds no /psci node. Recovery is external.
